1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,801
A new network engineer joins on Monday.

2
00:00:03,801 --> 00:00:06,535
By Thursday they still cannot log in to a

3
00:00:06,535 --> 00:00:10,070
single load balancer, and five tickets are sitting in

4
00:00:10,070 --> 00:00:14,004
five different queues, each waiting for someone to remember

5
00:00:14,004 --> 00:00:15,004
the right role.

6
00:00:15,754 --> 00:00:18,296
What if one agent read the joiner record,

7
00:00:18,296 --> 00:00:22,076
drafted every ticket, proposed every account with exactly the

8
00:00:22,076 --> 00:00:25,609
right privilege, and then waited for your approval before

9
00:00:25,609 --> 00:00:29,328
touching a device? That is credential and access management,

10
00:00:29,328 --> 00:00:31,187
done with Claude, done safely.

11
00:00:31,937 --> 00:00:37,337
Gennoor Tech presents Credential and Access Management Automation with

12
00:00:37,337 --> 00:00:37,877
Claude.

13
00:00:38,627 --> 00:00:42,230
One joiner in. Every account and every ticket out.

14
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:46,048
You build the workflow in ten increments across three

15
00:00:46,048 --> 00:00:49,723
days, and every increment is something you can run,

16
00:00:49,723 --> 00:00:53,181
review and demonstrate. Claude plans the access,

17
00:00:53,181 --> 00:00:56,208
drafts the tickets and explains each step.

18
00:00:56,208 --> 00:00:59,666
Deterministic Python code makes the A P I calls.

19
00:00:59,666 --> 00:01:03,485
A person approves anything that creates a credential.

20
00:01:03,485 --> 00:01:05,286
And everything is logged.

21
00:01:06,036 --> 00:01:08,387
You start with the real workflow.

22
00:01:08,387 --> 00:01:11,593
Who the joiner is, which team they belong to,

23
00:01:11,593 --> 00:01:14,443
and what that team is entitled to on F5,

24
00:01:14,443 --> 00:01:16,723
NetScaler, Radware, Cisco A C I,

25
00:01:16,723 --> 00:01:20,998
ServiceNow, GitHub and Terraform, plus other load balancers,

26
00:01:20,998 --> 00:01:24,561
Anaya L B included. You turn that tribal knowledge

27
00:01:24,561 --> 00:01:28,266
into a role-to-entitlement matrix that is versioned,

28
00:01:28,266 --> 00:01:29,762
owned and reviewable.

29
00:01:30,512 --> 00:01:32,498
Then you set up the tooling.

30
00:01:32,498 --> 00:01:34,768
Claude Code on your workstation,

31
00:01:34,768 --> 00:01:37,889
the Claude Agent S D K for the orchestrator,

32
00:01:37,889 --> 00:01:41,010
and M C P servers that expose ServiceNow and

33
00:01:41,010 --> 00:01:43,847
your identity source as read-only tools.

34
00:01:43,847 --> 00:01:47,181
You define structured J S O N outputs validated

35
00:01:47,181 --> 00:01:50,586
with Pydantic, so every access plan is an object

36
00:01:50,586 --> 00:01:52,785
with a schema, never free text.

37
00:01:52,785 --> 00:01:54,700
Feed it a malformed record,

38
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,466
or a request for a role the matrix does

39
00:01:57,466 --> 00:02:00,800
not grant, and it rejects with a reason instead

40
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:01,651
of guessing.

41
00:02:02,401 --> 00:02:04,359
Day two begins with ticketing.

42
00:02:04,359 --> 00:02:07,100
Using the ServiceNow Table A P I you raise

43
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:10,102
the request and one requested item per system,

44
00:02:10,102 --> 00:02:12,777
route each to the right fulfilment group,

45
00:02:12,777 --> 00:02:15,975
and let Flow Designer carry the manager approval.

46
00:02:15,975 --> 00:02:19,564
The agent writes the description and the justification.

47
00:02:19,564 --> 00:02:21,130
Your code owns the call,

48
00:02:21,130 --> 00:02:23,871
and it never raises the same ticket twice.

49
00:02:24,621 --> 00:02:28,826
Then the devices. Local accounts on F5 through iControl

50
00:02:28,826 --> 00:02:30,126
REST and t m s h,

51
00:02:30,126 --> 00:02:32,496
with partition access and role.

52
00:02:32,496 --> 00:02:36,089
System users on NetScaler through the NITRO A P

53
00:02:36,089 --> 00:02:39,835
I, bound to a command policy for least privilege.

54
00:02:39,835 --> 00:02:43,275
Users on Radware Alteon and Cyber Controller.

55
00:02:43,275 --> 00:02:46,715
Local users and security domains on Cisco A P

56
00:02:46,715 --> 00:02:50,003
I C. And an adapter interface so other load

57
00:02:50,003 --> 00:02:52,449
balancers, Anaya L B among them,

58
00:02:52,449 --> 00:02:55,660
plug in without changing the orchestrator,

59
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:58,871
or fall back to a ticket with exact manual

60
00:02:58,871 --> 00:03:02,464
instructions. Every account is a dry run first,

61
00:03:02,464 --> 00:03:05,369
with the exact request body on screen,

62
00:03:05,369 --> 00:03:08,580
then a gated apply, then a read-back and a

63
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:09,421
test login.

64
00:03:10,171 --> 00:03:14,261
Repository access is code. Team membership in GitHub is

65
00:03:14,261 --> 00:03:18,053
expressed in Terraform, opened as a pull request by

66
00:03:18,053 --> 00:03:22,142
Claude Code, planned by GitHub Actions and applied only

67
00:03:22,142 --> 00:03:25,860
after a reviewer merges. The joiner gets the right

68
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:28,314
teams and the right repositories,

69
00:03:28,314 --> 00:03:31,511
and the Terraform state file is the record.

70
00:03:32,261 --> 00:03:35,883
Day three is guardrails. Passwords are generated by code

71
00:03:35,883 --> 00:03:39,504
and delivered through a one-time channel the model never

72
00:03:39,504 --> 00:03:42,609
sees. Least privilege is enforced by the matrix,

73
00:03:42,609 --> 00:03:44,807
not by the prompt. Every approval,

74
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:45,907
every A P I call,

75
00:03:45,907 --> 00:03:49,399
every response and every verification is written to an

76
00:03:49,399 --> 00:03:52,180
append-only audit log kept with the ticket.

77
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:54,637
Then you verify the joiner end to end,

78
00:03:54,637 --> 00:03:57,742
send the hand-over, and run the same workflow in

79
00:03:57,742 --> 00:04:00,975
reverse for a leaver until every account and every

80
00:04:00,975 --> 00:04:02,527
team membership is gone.

81
00:04:03,277 --> 00:04:05,608
Every lab runs against a sandbox:

82
00:04:05,608 --> 00:04:10,481
a ServiceNow developer instance, virtual F5 and NetScaler appliances,

83
00:04:10,481 --> 00:04:13,376
a lab Radware controller, the Cisco A C I

84
